          <p>Social and Emotional Learning (SEL) is essential for addressing these challenges. SEL helps children and adults understand and manage emotions, set and achieve positive goals, feel and show empathy, maintain healthy relationships, and make responsible decisions.</p>
          <p>The National Education Policy (NEP) 2020 emphasizes the need for holistic student development and advocates for integrating life skills into education. It stresses that education should be "holistic, integrated, engaging, and enjoyable," requiring a shift beyond cognitive learning to also include affective and social-emotional domains.</p>

